  "notes": "F-242 (CL-BUG-160). Cross-tier strict-DER (BIP66) ECDSA signature vectors for every SDK's checkSig / ANF-interpreter verify path. Each vector is a 32-byte digest, a signature hex and the verdict under the pubkey below (Alice, priv e3b0c442...b855). Every ok=false vector is a RE-ENCODING of canonical_sig: it carries the same (r, s) integers, so a verifier that decodes it leniently verifies it as valid. Rejecting it is the only correct verdict: strict DER is consensus (BIP66 / SCRIPT_VERIFY_DERSIG), so OP_CHECKSIG on a node fails these, and an SDK that accepts them lets distinct byte strings stand for one signature. The *-control vectors prove each malformed vector differs from a valid signature ONLY in its encoding. A single trailing byte after the SEQUENCE is the sighash type and is stripped (canonical-plus-sighash-byte); anything else outside the canonical TLV is refused.",
